== 4. Section 1.2: the tilt inequality and the exponential weight ==
  [PASS] pointwise: every negative word with S_m > -y has Q(w) >= 2^(-hm) 2^(-lambda* y) (m <= 60, y in {1/2,1,2,4,8})
  [PASS] first inequality N_m(y) <= 2^(hm) 2^(lambda* y) Q(negative, S_m > -y) (exact N_m, 60-digit Q); min ratio bound/N = 1.00331
  [PASS] second inequality Q(neg, S_m > -y) <= e^(sy) E_Q[e^(sS_m); neg, S_m > -y] <= e^(sy) E_Q[e^(sS_m); neg] for s in {0.05, 0.1, 0.5}; min ratio full bound/N = 1.3582
  signs: lambda* > 0 and S_m > -y give the first; s > 0 and S_m + y > 0 on the event give e^(s(S_m+y)) >= 1 for the second; the integrand
  e^(sS_m) 1_(negative) is nonnegative so the constraint S_m > -y can be dropped.  Both directions correct.
