== 9. Consistency with THM-4487(2) ==
  [PASS] h'(rho*) = log_2((1-rho*)/rho*) = -alpha lambda*
  [PASS] concavity: h(rho(theta)) <= h* + lambda* theta for theta in (0, 0.1] (max h(rho) - h* - lambda* theta = -1.233e-8 < 0)
  [PASS] h(rho(theta)) > h* for theta in (0, 0.1] (rho < rho* < ... h decreasing on [1/2, 1]): THM-4487's fixed-theta exponent exceeds h*
  THM-4487(2): c X^(h(rho)) L^(-3/2) <= #F_b <= C X^(h(rho)) L^2.  Lemma 1.4c: #F_b <= 2|b| X^(0.585+theta) + 4 D_s X^(h* + lambda* theta + s theta/ln 2) L^(-3/2).
  upper >= lower needs h(rho) <= h* + lambda* theta + s theta/ln 2: true by concavity (strictly, for theta > 0). No contradiction; for fixed theta the
  lemma is WEAKER than THM-4487's upper bound in the exponent and only wins in the polynomial factor as theta -> 0: 'the ballot factor is a polynomial, not an exponent' is accurate.
